    "title": "Watch Artemis II splashdown livestream as crew returns to Earth",
    "text": "April 10, 2026, 11:45 a.m. ETAfter a historic mission to the moon, the Artemis II crew is set to return to Earth on Friday, April 10.The crew's 10-day trip around the moon will end when they splash down in the Pacific Ocean off the coast of San Diego, according to NASA. From the launch to the splashdown, the crew is expected to have traveled a total of 695,081 miles.They traveled farther from Earth than any human has before, venturing a maximum of 252,760 miles from our planet.At around 8:07 p.m. ET, the crew is expected to splash down in the Pacific, where NASA and U.S. Department of War personnel will help the crew climb out of their capsule, the Orion, and then fly them to a recovery ship.Watch live coverage of the astronauts' return home at the top of this story.USA TODAY's livestream of the splashdown will begin around 12 p.m. ET, which is about 25 minutes after the Artemis II crew is scheduled to wake up. The livestream can also be found on USA TODAY's YouTube channel. The mission can be tracked on NASA's website and on its mobile app.A look at the Artemis II schedule for April 10The splashdown is scheduled for about 8:07 p.m. ET on Friday, April 10, but preparations will begin hours before the astronauts return to Earth.The crew is scheduled to wake up and begin their day at 11:35 p.m., according to NASA. Then, at 1:50 p.m., the Orion cabin will be configured for the crew's reentry to Earth's atmosphere.NASA's coverage of the splashdown will then go live at 6:30 p.m. ET, and the Orion is scheduled to reenter Earth's atmosphere at 7:53 p.m. ET.Finally, the splashdown will take place at 8:07 p.m. ET, followed by a post-splashdown news conference at NASA's Lyndon B. Johnson Space Center in Houston, Texas, at 10:30 p.m. ET.Julia Gomez is a Trending reporter for USA TODAY and covers popular toys, space phenomena, scientific studies, natural disasters, holidays, and trending news. Connect with her on LinkedIn, X, Instagram, and TikTok: @juliamariegz, or email her at jgomez@gannett.com.",
